Z||000000||86SEFIERO||02-05-2001||02:45 AM||||<BR>I would like to know how the notchback rear roof section was installed onto the Gt body? I want a GT car but I dont like the looks of the Gt rear winow panels. I was also wondering if you have the chop top conversion as a kit yet!Thanks!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||02-05-2001||05:47 AM||||The Notchback effect was a total custom thing, I can't remember where I read that though.<BR>It was a fastback section that was customized, notice the fastback tail lights.<P>Just my $.02  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">    <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-05-2001||09:27 AM||||The notchback isn't a notchback panel. The original owner (Rich Warber) sculpted them using the GT panel. If you notice in the pics it is curved not straight edged like a notchback. Archie can do choptops I don't think he sells it as a kit since it uses youe exsisting parts. (windshield,roof,etc)<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||HarryG||02-05-2001||12:15 PM||||Archie; <BR>Another question on the PPE;<BR>I see the owner used a Fluidampr balancer.<BR>How did he fit that in? Cut the frame, move the engine to the left, or both?||||reg||5
Z||000004||Archie||02-05-2001||07:58 PM||||As you may know, the PPE was owned by the late Rich Warber (who also worked for me until he passed on). When first assembled, Rich's car was a Black Chopped GT Fastback body style, real similar to my Blue Chop Top car. He drove it occasionally on the street, but mostly he kept it real nice for a show car. He showed the car everytime he could and ALWAYS, yes, ALWAYS won a 1st place trophy in every show it was in & many time he would also win BOS. <P>Anyway a couple of years ago (in what turned out to be the last show the car was ever entered in) Rich got a 2nd place. He didn't take that well at all. You & I would have entered another show or 2 to see if this 2nd. place stuff was a fluke or a trend. Not Rich, He went right home and started making plans to change the car once again and had started modifying the car by the Monday after the 2nd. place finish. That is when he did the notchback chopped roof on the GT rear clip. Just a couple of days after that show Rich, without telling me what he was up to, took one of my used (extra) notchback rear sections home from work. He then removed the sail panels from the tops of his GT fenders (leaving the GT decklid as it was) and grafted on the "B" pillars from that notchback rear clip. He also made a few other changes like that "wickerbill" at the trailing edge of the roof above the rear window. Rich also picked the intended paint color and almost completed the body prep for paint when he became too sick to work on it anymore.  Several months after his death the members of the Chicago Area NIFE Club got together and finished the car just as Rich would have done it had he had the chance.<P>Archie<P>This is how it looked before the n'back conversion.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/131.jpg"> <P>This is after the N'Back conversion<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/16_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
